","options":["language","idiom","country","word"]},"answer":"language","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-el-idioma"]},{"id":"es-b1-u01-l03-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u01-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Hablo tres ___: español, inglés y francés.","translation":"I speak three languages: Spanish, English and French.","options":["idiomas","países","veces","ciudades"]},"answer":"idiomas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Languages are idiomas. El idioma is masculine although it ends in -a: el idioma, los idiomas.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-el-idioma"]},{"id":"es-b1-u01-l03-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u01-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"En este viaje he conocido ___ mucha gente.","translation":"On this trip I have met a lot of people.","options":["a","de","en","con"]},"answer":"a","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"When the object of conocer is a person, Spanish adds a: he conocido a mucha gente. With a place there is no a: he conocido Mérida.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-he-conocido"]},{"id":"es-b1-u01-l03-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u01-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Fui a Mérida por ___ vez en 2021.","translation":"I went to Mérida for the first time in 2021.","options":["primera","primer","una","varias"]},"answer":"primera","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Vez is feminine, so it is primera vez. Notice the preterite fui: the sentence gives a date (en 2021).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-por-primera-vez"]},{"id":"es-b1-u01-l03-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u01-l03","position":5,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prom