:12,"words":["es-es-necesario-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Es necesario que ___ inglés para este puesto.","translation":"You need to know English for this position. (formal)","options":["sepa","sabe","saber"]},"answer":"sepa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Saber has an irregular subjunctive: sepa, sepas, sepa… With usted the form is sepa. Sabe is the ordinary present.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-es-necesario-que","es-el-puesto"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":3,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Es importante que llegues a tiempo.","options":["Es importante que llegues a tiempo.","Es importante llegar a tiempo.","Es importante que llegue a tiempo."]},"answer":"Es importante que llegues a tiempo.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-es-importante-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Es importante que el cliente ___ contento.","translation":"It’s important that the customer is happy.","options":["esté","está","sea","estar"]},"answer":"esté","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Contento goes with estar, and after es importante que you need the subjunctive of estar: esté (with an accent). Sea is the subjunctive of ser.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-es-importante-que","es-el-cliente"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Es necesario que ___ al banco hoy.","translation":"It’s necessary that you go to the bank today.","options":["vayas","vas","ir","fuiste"]},"answer":"vayas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ir has an irregular subjunctive: vaya, vayas (tú), vaya… Vas is the ordinary present.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-es-necesario-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":6,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"es necesario que","right":"it's necessary that"},{"left":"solicitar","right":"to apply for"},{"left":"el cliente","right":"the client"},{"left":"el turno","right":"the shift"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-es-necesario-que","es-solicitar","es-el-cliente","es-el-turno"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u5-anuncio","document":"ad","setting":"A job ad from a hotel in Guadalajara.","title":"Buscamos recepcionista","lines":["Hotel en Guadalajara busca recepcionista para el turno de la tarde.","Es necesario que hable inglés y que tenga experiencia con clientes.","También es importante que sepa usar la computadora y que pueda trabajar los sábados.","El turno es de martes a sábado, de las dos de la tarde a las diez de la noche.","El sueldo es de doce mil pesos al mes.","Para solicitar el puesto, mande su currículum antes del 15 de marzo."]},"question":"Which shift is the job for?","options":["The afternoon shift, from 2 to 10 p.m.","The morning shift","The night shift, from 10 p.m.","Only weekends"]},"answer":"The afternoon shift, from 2 to 10 p.m.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The ad says “busca recepcionista para el turno de la tarde” and “de las dos de la tarde a las diez de la noche”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":8,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u5-anuncio","document":"ad","setting":"A job ad from a hotel in Guadalajara.","title":"Buscamos recepcionista","lines":["Hotel en Guadalajara busca recepcionista para el turno de la tarde.","Es necesario que hable inglés y que tenga experiencia con clientes.","También es importante que sepa usar la computadora y que pueda trabajar los sábados.","El turno es de martes a sábado, de las dos de la tarde a las diez de la noche.","El sueldo es de doce mil pesos al mes.","Para solicitar el puesto, mande su currículum antes del 15 de marzo."]},"question":"What is necessary for the job?","options":["Speaking English and having experience with customers","Having a university degree","Living in the center","Working on Sundays"]},"answer":"Speaking English and having experience with customers","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The ad says “Es necesario que hable inglés y que tenga experiencia con clientes”. Hable and tenga are subjunctives.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"It’s important that you get to your shift on time."},"answer":"Es importante que llegues a tiempo a tu turno.","accepted_answers":["Es importante que llegues a tu turno a tiempo.","Es importante que llegues temprano a tu turno.","Es importante que llegue a tiempo a su turno.","Es importante que usted llegue a tiempo a su turno."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-es-importante-que","es-el-turno"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l02-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l02","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Qué es necesario para el puesto?","translation":"Say it is necessary that the person speaks English (start with «Es necesario que»)."},"answer":"Es necesario que hable inglés.","accepted_answers":["Es necesario que hable inglés","Es necesario que sepa inglés.","Es necesario que hable inglés muy bien.","Es necesario que hables inglés.","Es necesario que sepas inglés."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-es-necesario-que","es-el-puesto"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":1,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"el jefe","options":["el jefe","el cliente","renunciar","contratar"]},"answer":"el jefe","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-el-jefe"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Es necesario que ___ inglés para este puesto.","translation":"You need to know English for this position. (formal)","options":["sepa","sabe","saber"]},"answer":"sepa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Saber has an irregular subjunctive: sepa, sepas, sepa… With usted the form is sepa. Sabe is the ordinary present.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-es-necesario-que","es-el-puesto"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":3,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Write the whole word","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"e_ i_p_r_a_t_ q_e","hint":"it's important that"},"answer":"es importante que","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["es-es-importante-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Mi jefe quiere que ___ a las ocho.","translation":"My boss wants me to arrive at eight.","options":["llegue","llego","llegar","llegaste"]},"answer":"llegue","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Two subjects (my boss wants / I arrive), so que + subjunctive: llegue. The g becomes gu to keep the hard sound: llegar → llegue.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-quiero-que","es-el-jefe"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":5,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “el cliente” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"el cliente","options":["the client","it's necessary that","the degree (course)","the scholarship"]},"answer":"the client","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-el-cliente"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":6,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"el cliente","right":"the client"},{"left":"el jefe","right":"the boss"},{"left":"es importante que","right":"it's important that"},{"left":"es necesario que","right":"it's necessary that"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-el-cliente","es-el-jefe","es-es-importante-que","es-es-necesario-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":7,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Qué es necesario para el puesto?","translation":"Say it is necessary that the person speaks English (start with «Es necesario que»)."},"answer":"Es necesario que hable inglés.","accepted_answers":["Es necesario que hable inglés","Es necesario que sepa inglés.","Es necesario que hable inglés muy bien.","Es necesario que hables inglés.","Es necesario que sepas inglés."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-es-necesario-que","es-el-puesto"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":8,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “quiero que” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"quiero que","options":["I want (someone) to","dear (formal)","to apply for","to hire"]},"answer":"I want (someone) to","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-quiero-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Qué quiere tu jefe?","translation":"Say your boss wants you to work on Saturday (start with «Quiere que»)."},"answer":"Quiere que trabaje el sábado.","accepted_answers":["Quiere que trabaje el sábado","Quiere que trabaje los sábados.","Mi jefe quiere que trabaje el sábado.","Quiere que yo trabaje el sábado.","Quiere que trabaje este sábado."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-quiero-que","es-el-jefe"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-rev1","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"it's necessary that"},"answer":"es necesario que","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-es-necesario-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “contratar” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"contratar","options":["to hire","to apply for","to pay","to meet"]},"answer":"to hire","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-contratar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Terminé la ___ de medicina el año pasado.","translation":"I finished my medical degree last year.","options":["carrera","oficina","entrevista","reunión"]},"answer":"carrera","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"La carrera is the whole university program: la carrera de medicina, de ingeniería. El título is the diploma you get at the end.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-la-carrera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":3,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"¿Qué carrera estudió?","options":["¿Qué carrera estudió?","¿Qué carrera estudias?","¿Dónde estudió?"]},"answer":"¿Qué carrera estudió?","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-la-carrera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u5-entrevista","setting":"A job interview at a company in Monterrey. Javier, the manager, and Valeria, the candidate, use usted.","speakers":[{"name":"Javier","voice":"a"},{"name":"Valeria","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Buenos días, Valeria. Siéntese, por favor. ¿Qué carrera estudió?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Soy ingeniera. Terminé la carrera el año pasado en Monterrey."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"¿Y por qué quiere trabajar con nosotros?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Porque es una empresa grande y me gusta mucho trabajar con clientes."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Bien. En este puesto va a hablar con clientes de Estados Unidos, así que es necesario que sepa inglés."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"No hay problema: viví dos años en Chicago y hablo inglés todos los días."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Perfecto. Queremos contratar a alguien este mes. La llamo el viernes."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Muchas gracias, señor. Entonces espero que me llame el viernes."}]},"question":"What did Valeria study?","options":["Engineering","Medicine","English","She didn’t go to university"]},"answer":"Engineering","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Valeria answers “Soy ingeniera. Terminé la carrera el año pasado”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u5-entrevista","setting":"A job interview at a company in Monterrey. Javier, the manager, and Valeria, the candidate, use usted.","speakers":[{"name":"Javier","voice":"a"},{"name":"Valeria","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Buenos días, Valeria. Siéntese, por favor. ¿Qué carrera estudió?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Soy ingeniera. Terminé la carrera el año pasado en Monterrey."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"¿Y por qué quiere trabajar con nosotros?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Porque es una empresa grande y me gusta mucho trabajar con clientes."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Bien. En este puesto va a hablar con clientes de Estados Unidos, así que es necesario que sepa inglés."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"No hay problema: viví dos años en Chicago y hablo inglés todos los días."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Perfecto. Queremos contratar a alguien este mes. La llamo el viernes."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Muchas gracias, señor. Entonces espero que me llame el viernes."}]},"question":"Why does Valeria need to know English?","options":["She will talk to clients from the United States","She will live in Chicago","Her boss doesn’t speak Spanish","She has to write the reports in English"]},"answer":"She will talk to clients from the United States","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Javier says “va a hablar con clientes de Estados Unidos, así que es necesario que sepa inglés”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u5-entrevista","setting":"A job interview at a company in Monterrey. Javier, the manager, and Valeria, the candidate, use usted.","speakers":[{"name":"Javier","voice":"a"},{"name":"Valeria","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Buenos días, Valeria. Siéntese, por favor. ¿Qué carrera estudió?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Soy ingeniera. Terminé la carrera el año pasado en Monterrey."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"¿Y por qué quiere trabajar con nosotros?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Porque es una empresa grande y me gusta mucho trabajar con clientes."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Bien. En este puesto va a hablar con clientes de Estados Unidos, así que es necesario que sepa inglés."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"No hay problema: viví dos años en Chicago y hablo inglés todos los días."},{"speaker":"Javier","text":"Perfecto. Queremos contratar a alguien este mes. La llamo el viernes."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Muchas gracias, señor. Entonces espero que me llame el viernes."}]},"question":"What does Javier say at the end?","options":["They want to hire someone this month and he will call her on Friday","She has the job and starts on Monday","They don’t want to hire anyone this year","She has to come back for another interview tomorrow"]},"answer":"They want to hire someone this month and he will call her on Friday","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Javier says “Queremos contratar a alguien este mes. La llamo el viernes.” La is the object pronoun for usted when you speak to a woman.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":7,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"La empresa quiere ___ a dos ingenieros.","translation":"The company wants to hire two engineers.","options":["contratar","trabajar","solicitar","llegar"]},"answer":"contratar","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Contratar a + person: to hire someone. Solicitar is what the candidate does (to apply for a job), not the company.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-contratar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":8,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"contratar","right":"to hire"},{"left":"la carrera","right":"the degree (course)"},{"left":"el cliente","right":"the client"},{"left":"solicitar","right":"to apply for"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-contratar","es-la-carrera","es-el-cliente","es-solicitar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"I hope the company hires me."},"answer":"Espero que la empresa me contrate.","accepted_answers":["Espero que me contrate la empresa.","Ojalá que la empresa me contrate.","Ojalá la empresa me contrate."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-espero-que","es-contratar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l03-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l03","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Qué carrera estudió?","translation":"You are in a job interview. Say you studied engineering (start with «Estudié»)."},"answer":"Estudié ingeniería.","accepted_answers":["Estudié ingeniería","Estudié la carrera de ingeniería.","Estudié ingeniería en la universidad.","Estudié la carrera de ingeniería"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-la-carrera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l04-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l04","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “el ascenso” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"el ascenso","options":["the promotion","the elevator","the shift","the deadline"]},"answer":"the promotion","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-el-ascenso"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l04-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ señora Pérez: Le escribo para solicitar el puesto.","translation":"Dear Mrs. Pérez, I am writing to apply for the position.","options":["Estimada","Estimado","Atentamente","Hola"]},"answer":"Estimada","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Estimado agrees with the person: estimado señor, estimada señora. Atentamente goes at the end of the email, and hola is too informal here.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-estimado","es-solicitar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l04-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l04","position":3,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Le escribo para solicitar el puesto.","options":["Le escribo para solicitar el puesto.","Le escribo para renunciar al puesto.","Les escribo para solicitar el puesto."]},"answer":"Le escribo para solicitar el puesto.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-solicitar","es-renunciar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l04-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Si no me dan el ascenso, voy a ___.","translation":"If they don’t give me the promotion, I’m going to quit.","options":["renunciar","contratar","solicitar","llegar"]},"answer":"renunciar","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Renunciar is to resign or quit a job (renunciar a un puesto). Contratar is what the company does when it hires you.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-renunciar","es-el-ascenso"]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l04-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u05-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u5-correo","document":"email","setting":"Mónica, the head of a sales team in Bogotá, writes to her team.","from":"Mónica","lines":["Estimado equipo:","Les escribo para contarles dos cosas importantes.","Primero, como ya saben, Rodrigo renunció a su puesto la semana pasada porque se muda a Lima.","Por eso, desde el lunes Paola es la nueva jefa del equipo: ¡felicidades por el ascenso, Paola!","También, el informe del proyecto tiene una fecha límite: el viernes 20.","Es necesario que cada uno haga su parte antes del jueves, porque quiero que lo revisemos juntos el viernes por la mañana.","Muchas gracias por su trabajo.","Atentamente, Mónica"]},"question":"Why is Rodrigo leaving the team?","options":["He resigned because he is moving to Lima","He got a promotion","The company didn’t want him","He is going to study in Bogotá"]},"answer":"He resigned because he is moving to Lima","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mónica writes “Rodrigo renunció a su puesto la semana pasada porque se muda a Lima”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u05-l04-e06","les