e":"The more I sleep, the better I feel."},"answer":"Cuanto más duermo, mejor me siento.","accepted_answers":["Cuanto más duermo mejor me siento.","Mientras más duermo, mejor me siento.","Mientras más duermo mejor me siento.","Cuanto más duermo, me siento mejor."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-cuanto-mas"]},{"id":"es-b1-u07-l03-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u07-l03","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Por qué estás agotada?","translation":"Say you have a lot of stress at work (start with «Tengo»)."},"answer":"Tengo mucho estrés en el trabajo.","accepted_answers":["Tengo mucho estrés en el trabajo","Tengo mucho estrés.","Tengo mucho estrés en mi trabajo.","Tengo mucho estrés en la oficina.","Tengo cada vez más estrés en el trabajo.","Porque tengo mucho estrés en el trabajo."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-el-estres","es-agotado"]},{"id":"es-b1-u07-l04-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u07-l04","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “me preocupa que” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"me preocupa que","options":["it worries me that","I hope that","I want (someone) to","it would be better"]},"answer":"it worries me that","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-me-preocupa-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u07-l04-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u07-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Me preocupa que no ___ bien.","translation":"It worries me that you don’t sleep well.","options":["duermas","duermes","dormir"]},"answer":"duermas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Me preocupa que + another person takes the subjunctive: duermes → duermas. The infinitive dormir only works without que (me preocupa dormir poco).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-me-preocupa-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u07-l04-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u07-l04","position":3,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"me preocupa que","right":"it worries me that"},{"left":"cuidarse","right":"to look after oneself"},{"left":"meditar","right":"to meditate"},{"left":"el estrés","right":"stress"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-me-preocupa-que","es-cuidarse","es-meditar","es-el-estres"]},{"id":"es-b1-u07-l04-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u07-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u7-estres","setting":"Adriana and Paola, two friends who work in the same office in Mexico City, talk at lunchtime.","speakers":[{"name":"Adriana","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paola","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Paola, te veo muy cansada. ¿Estás bien?"},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"No mucho. Tengo mucho estrés en el trabajo y duermo muy mal."},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Me preocupa que trabajes tantas horas. Ayer saliste de la oficina a las diez."},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"Es que mi jefe quiere el proyecto para el viernes."},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Te entiendo, pero tienes que cuidarte. Yo que tú, hablaría con él."},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"Tienes razón. ¿Y tú qué haces cuando tienes estrés?"},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Medito diez minutos todas las mañanas. Cuanto más medito, más tranquila estoy."},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"¿Meditar? Nunca lo he probado."},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Es fácil. Esta noche te mando una app para empezar."}]},"question":"What worries Adriana?","options":["That Paola works so many hours","That Paola eats badly","That Paola wants to change jobs","That Paola smokes"]},"answer":"That Paola works so many hours","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Adriana says “Me preocupa que trabajes tantas horas” and adds that Paola left the office at ten.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u07-l04-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u07-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u7-estres","setting":"Adriana and Paola, two friends who work in the same office in Mexico City, talk at lunchtime.","speakers":[{"name":"Adriana","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paola","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Paola, te veo muy cansada. ¿Estás bien?"},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"No mucho. Tengo mucho estrés en el trabajo y duermo muy mal."},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Me preocupa que trabajes tantas horas. Ayer saliste de la oficina a las diez."},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"Es que mi jefe quiere el proyecto para el viernes."},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Te entiendo, pero tienes que cuidarte. Yo que tú, hablaría con él."},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"Tienes razón. ¿Y tú qué haces cuando tienes estrés?"},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Medito diez minutos todas las mañanas. Cuanto más medito, más tranquila estoy."},{"speaker":"Paola","text":"¿Meditar? Nunca lo he probado."},{"speaker":"Adriana","text":"Es fácil. Esta noche te mando una app para empezar."}]},"question":"What does Adriana advise Paola to do?","options":["To talk to her boss","To finish the project on Friday","To change offices","To go to the doctor"]},"answer":"To talk to her boss","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"She says “tienes que cuidarte. Yo que tú, hablaría con él”, and él is Paola’s boss.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u07-l04-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u07-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload"