,"options":["Because of a storm","Because of a fire","Because it is very hot","Because of a football final"]},"answer":"Because of a storm","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The headline says “Tormenta en Veracruz: hoy no hay clases en las escuelas”. The fire is in Monterrey and the heat in Mérida.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l01-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l01","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u10-titulares","document":"notice","setting":"The morning headlines in a news app.","title":"Las noticias de hoy","lines":["Monterrey: gran incendio en una fábrica del centro","Tormenta en Veracruz: hoy no hay clases en las escuelas","El gobierno de Bogotá quiere más bicicletas en la ciudad","Fútbol: Monterrey llega a la final","Mérida: mañana va a hacer mucho calor"]},"question":"What does the government of Bogotá want?","options":["More bicycles in the city","A new factory","More schools","Fewer cars at night"]},"answer":"More bicycles in the city","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The headline says “El gobierno de Bogotá quiere más bicicletas en la ciudad”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l01-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l01","position":8,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Hubo un ___ en una fábrica del centro.","translation":"There was a fire in a factory downtown.","options":["incendio","tormenta","titular","gobierno"]},"answer":"incendio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A fire that burns a building or a forest is el incendio (un incendio). La tormenta is a storm; it is feminine, so it would be “una tormenta”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-el-incendio"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l01-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l01","position":9,"type":"translate_w