osition":2,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"explicó que","right":"explained that"},{"left":"contó que","right":"told (that)"},{"left":"el testigo","right":"witness"},{"left":"el periodista","right":"journalist"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-explico-que","es-conto-que","es-el-testigo","es-el-periodista"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"La jefa explicó que el proyecto ___ muy importante.","translation":"The boss explained that the project was very important.","options":["era","sea","ser","son"]},"answer":"era","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In reported speech the present moves back to the imperfect: “es importante” → explicó que era importante. (If it is still true, you will also hear explicó que es importante.)","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-explico-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Explicó que ___ a llover por la tarde.","translation":"He explained that it was going to rain in the afternoon.","options":["iba","ir","vas","iban"]},"answer":"iba","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Va a llover becomes iba a llover in reported speech. Llover is impersonal (there is no subject, like “it rains”), so iba stays singular.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-explico-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"«El cliente vendrá el lunes». → Contó que el cliente ___ el lunes.","translation":"“The client will come on Monday.” → She said the client would come on Monday.","options":["vendría","venir","vine","vienes"]},"answer":"vendría","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The future (vendrá) becomes the conditional (vendría, “would come”) in reported speech. Vine is “I came”, and vienes is “you come”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-conto-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Explicó que era muy tarde.","options":["Explicó que era muy tarde.","Explicó que era muy temprano.","Contó que era muy tarde.","Explicó que es muy tarde."]},"answer":"Explicó que era muy tarde.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-explico-que","es-conto-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u10-articulo","document":"description","setting":"A newspaper article the day after the storm.","title":"El día después de la tormenta","lines":["La tormenta de Veracruz terminó ayer por la tarde.","Según el gobierno, más de 300 casas tienen problemas con el agua.","Una testigo, Rosa, contó que el agua llegó a su cocina en diez minutos.","Su vecino explicó que era la tormenta más fuerte del año.","El gobierno anunció que las escuelas iban a abrir el lunes.","Hoy ya hay sol en la ciudad."]},"question":"What did Rosa tell the newspaper?","options":["That the water reached her kitchen in ten minutes","That it was the strongest storm of the year","That 300 houses have problems with water","That the schools were going to open on Monday"]},"answer":"That the water reached her kitchen in ten minutes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The article says “Una testigo, Rosa, contó que el agua llegó a su cocina en diez minutos”. The strongest storm of the year is what her neighbor explained.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":8,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u10-articulo","document":"description","setting":"A newspaper article the day after the storm.","title":"El día después de la tormenta","lines":["La tormenta de Veracruz terminó ayer por la tarde.","Según el gobierno, más de 300 casas tienen problemas con el agua.","Una testigo, Rosa, contó que el agua llegó a su cocina en diez minutos.","Su vecino explicó que era la tormenta más fuerte del año.","El gobierno anunció que las escuelas iban a abrir el lunes.","Hoy ya hay sol en la ciudad."]},"question":"What did the government announce?","options":["That the schools were going to open on Monday","That the storm was going to come back","That families had to leave their houses","That there was no sun in the city"]},"answer":"That the schools were going to open on Monday","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The article says “El gobierno anunció que las escuelas iban a abrir el lunes”: van a abrir → iban a abrir.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"She explained that it was very important."},"answer":"Explicó que era muy importante.","accepted_answers":["Ella explicó que era muy importante.","Explicó que es muy importante.","Ella explicó que es muy importante."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-explico-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l03-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"The witness said that the fire was very big."},"answer":"El testigo contó que el incendio era muy grande.","accepted_answers":["La testigo contó que el incendio era muy grande.","El testigo dijo que el incendio era muy grande.","La testigo dijo que el incendio era muy grande.","El testigo explicó que el incendio era muy grande.","El testigo contó que el incendio fue muy grande.","El testigo dijo que el incendio fue muy grande."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-el-testigo","es-conto-que","es-el-incendio"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “me pidió que” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"me pidió que","options":["asked me to","asked me if","told (that)","explained that"]},"answer":"asked me to","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-me-pidio-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Me ___ si tenía tiempo.","translation":"She asked me if I had time.","options":["preguntó","pidió","contó","explicó"]},"answer":"preguntó","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A question is reported with preguntar: me preguntó si… Pedir is for requests (me pidió que + subjunctive).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-me-pregunto-si"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Mi jefa me pidió que le ___ el archivo.","translation":"My boss asked me to send her the file.","options":["mande","mando","mandar","manda"]},"answer":"mande","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Pedir que + subjunctive: mande (from mandar: -ar verbs take -e). Mando and manda are indicative, and the infinitive mandar needs no que.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-me-pidio-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Me preguntó ___ vivía.","translation":"He asked me where I lived.","options":["dónde","si","que","según"]},"answer":"dónde","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A reported question with a question word keeps the word and its accent: “¿Dónde vives?” → me preguntó dónde vivía. Si is only for yes / no questions.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-me-pregunto-si"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":5,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Me preguntó si tenía tiempo.","options":["Me preguntó si tenía tiempo.","Me preguntó si tenía frío.","Me dijo que tenía tiempo.","Me preguntó si tienes tiempo."]},"answer":"Me preguntó si tenía tiempo.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-me-pregunto-si"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u10-testigo","setting":"A journalist talks to a woman who saw a fire in a factory in Monterrey.","speakers":[{"name":"Sergio","voice":"a"},{"name":"Gloria","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"Buenos días, señora. Soy periodista. ¿Usted vio el incendio de la fábrica?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"Sí, vivo enfrente. A las seis de la mañana vi mucho humo y llamé a los bomberos."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"¿Y qué le preguntaron los bomberos?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"Me preguntaron si había personas en la fábrica. Yo no sabía."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"¿Y había alguien?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"No, por suerte. Un señor de la fábrica me contó que todos llegan a las ocho."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"¿Y ahora qué tiene que hacer la gente del barrio?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"Un bombero me pidió que cierre las ventanas y que no salga de casa hoy."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"Muchas gracias por su tiempo, señora."}]},"question":"What did the firefighters ask Gloria?","options":["If there were people in the factory","Where she lived","When the fire started","If she could close the factory"]},"answer":"If there were people in the factory","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Gloria says “Me preguntaron si había personas en la fábrica”: preguntar + si for a yes / no question.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u10-testigo","setting":"A journalist talks to a woman who saw a fire in a factory in Monterrey.","speakers":[{"name":"Sergio","voice":"a"},{"name":"Gloria","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"Buenos días, señora. Soy periodista. ¿Usted vio el incendio de la fábrica?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"Sí, vivo enfrente. A las seis de la mañana vi mucho humo y llamé a los bomberos."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"¿Y qué le preguntaron los bomberos?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"Me preguntaron si había personas en la fábrica. Yo no sabía."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"¿Y había alguien?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"No, por suerte. Un señor de la fábrica me contó que todos llegan a las ocho."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"¿Y ahora qué tiene que hacer la gente del barrio?"},{"speaker":"Gloria","text":"Un bombero me pidió que cierre las ventanas y que no salga de casa hoy."},{"speaker":"Sergio","text":"Muchas gracias por su tiempo, señora."}]},"question":"What did a firefighter ask Gloria to do?","options":["Close the windows and stay at home today","Call the newspaper","Leave the neighborhood","Talk to the workers of the factory"]},"answer":"Close the windows and stay at home today","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Gloria says “Un bombero me pidió que cierre las ventanas y que no salga de casa hoy”: pedir que + subjunctive.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":8,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u10-reunion","document":"message","setting":"Inés writes to her colleague Pablo, who missed a meeting.","from":"Inés","to":"Pablo","lines":["Hola, Pablo. Te cuento lo que pasó en la reunión de hoy.","La jefa explicó que el proyecto era muy importante para el cliente.","Contó que el cliente vendría a la oficina el lunes.","También dijo que íbamos a trabajar en equipo toda la semana.","Me preguntó si tú podías presentar el proyecto el lunes. Le dije que no sabía.","Y me pidió que te mande el archivo de la reunión: te lo mando esta noche.","Según ella, la fecha límite es el viernes. ¡Hablamos mañana!"]},"question":"What did the boss ask Inés?","options":["If Pablo could present the project on Monday","If Inés could send the file to the client","Where Pablo was","When the client was going to come"]},"answer":"If Pablo could present the project on Monday","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Inés writes “Me preguntó si tú podías presentar el proyecto el lunes”: the boss asked if Pablo could (¿puede…?), and Inés, writing to Pablo, reports it with tú: si podías.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"She asked me to call her tomorrow."},"answer":"Me pidió que la llame mañana.","accepted_answers":["Ella me pidió que la llame mañana.","Me pidió que la llamara mañana.","Ella me pidió que la llamara mañana.","Me pidió que la llamase mañana."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-me-pidio-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-l04-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-l04","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"«¿Tienes tiempo mañana?», te preguntó Ana. ¿Qué te preguntó?","translation":"Report Ana’s question (use «me preguntó si»)."},"answer":"Me preguntó si tenía tiempo mañana.","accepted_answers":["Me preguntó si tenía tiempo.","Me preguntó si tengo tiempo mañana.","Ana me preguntó si tenía tiempo mañana.","Me preguntó si tenía tiempo al día siguiente.","Ana me preguntó si tengo tiempo mañana."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-me-pregunto-si"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-rev2-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-rev2","position":1,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"el periodista","options":["el periodista","explicó que","las noticias","el testigo"]},"answer":"el periodista","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-el-periodista"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-rev2-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-rev2","position":2,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"She asked me to call her tomorrow."},"answer":"Me pidió que la llame mañana.","accepted_answers":["Ella me pidió que la llame mañana.","Me pidió que la llamara mañana.","Ella me pidió que la llamara mañana.","Me pidió que la llamase mañana."],"explanation_e