"},"answer":"el artículo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-el-articulo"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-final-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-final","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Hubo un ___ en una fábrica del centro.","translation":"There was a fire in a factory downtown.","options":["incendio","tormenta","titular","gobierno"]},"answer":"incendio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A fire that burns a building or a forest is el incendio (un incendio). La tormenta is a storm; it is feminine, so it would be “una tormenta”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-el-incendio"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-final-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-final","position":6,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Put the words in order","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["El","periodista","me","preguntó","dónde","vivía"],"translation":"The journalist asked me where I lived."},"answer":"El periodista me preguntó dónde vivía.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["es-el-periodista","es-me-pregunto-si"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-final-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-final","position":7,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"«El cliente vendrá el lunes». → Contó que el cliente ___ el lunes.","translation":"“The client will come on Monday.” → She said the client would come on Monday.","options":["vendría","venir","vine","vienes"]},"answer":"vendría","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The future (vendrá) becomes the conditional (vendría, “would come”) in reported speech. Vine is “I came”, and vienes is “you come”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-conto-que"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-final-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-final","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"anunciar","options":["anunciar","el testigo","la tormenta","el incendio"]},"answer":"anunciar","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-anunciar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-final-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-final","position":9,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Me preguntó ___ vivía.","translation":"He asked me where I lived.","options":["dónde","si","que","según"]},"answer":"dónde","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A reported question with a question word keeps the word and its accent: “¿Dónde vives?” → me preguntó dónde vivía. Si is only for yes / no questions.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-me-pregunto-si"]},{"id":"es-b1-u10-final-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u10-final","position":10,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “según” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"según","options":["according to","newspaper","asked me to","the news"]},"answer":"according to","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-segun"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “la ventaja” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"la ventaja","options":["advantage","disadvantage","opinion","solution"]},"answer":"advantage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-la-ventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":2,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “opinar” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"opinar","options":["to give an opinion","to argue","to agree","to convince"]},"answer":"to give an opinion","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-opinar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":3,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"la ventaja","right":"advantage"},{"left":"la desventaja","right":"disadvantage"},{"left":"por un lado","right":"on the one hand"},{"left":"por otro lado","right":"on the other hand"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-la-ventaja","es-la-desventaja","es-por-un-lado","es-por-otro-lado"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Por un lado, el apartamento es barato; por ___ lado, está muy lejos.","translation":"On the one hand, the apartment is cheap; on the other hand, it’s very far away.","options":["otro","un","el","mi"]},"answer":"otro","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The second argument is introduced by por otro lado. Por un lado only opens the first one, so it isn’t repeated.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-por-otro-lado","es-por-un-lado"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"La ___ del campo es que no hay cines.","translation":"The disadvantage of the countryside is that there are no cinemas.","options":["desventaja","ventaja","solución","cuenta"]},"answer":"desventaja","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Having no cinemas is a negative point: la desventaja. Des- gives the opposite meaning, like English dis-.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-la-desventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Una ventaja es el precio.","options":["Una ventaja es el precio.","Una desventaja es el precio.","Una ventaja es el clima.","La ventaja es el precio."]},"answer":"Una ventaja es el precio.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-la-ventaja","es-la-desventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":7,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Creo que la ciudad tiene más ___.","translation":"I think the city has more advantages.","options":["ventajas","ventaja","desventaja"]},"answer":"ventajas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"After más with something you can count, use the plural, as in English: más ventajas (more advantages).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-la-ventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Put the words in order","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Mi","papá","siempre","quiere","opinar"],"translation":"My dad always wants to give his opinion."},"answer":"Mi papá siempre quiere opinar.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["es-opinar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"On the one hand, it’s cheap; on the other hand, it’s far away."},"answer":"Por un lado, es barato; por otro lado, está lejos.","accepted_answers":["Por un lado es barato; por otro lado está lejos.","Por un lado, es barato, por otro lado, está lejos.","Por un lado es barato, por otro lado está lejos.","Por un lado, es barato. Por otro lado, está lejos.","Por un lado, es barata; por otro lado, está lejos.","Por un lado, es barato; por otro lado, queda lejos."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-por-un-lado","es-por-otro-lado"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l01-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l01","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Cuál es una ventaja de la ciudad?","translation":"Name one advantage of the city (start with «Una ventaja es…»)."},"answer":"Una ventaja es el metro.","accepted_answers":["Una ventaja es el trabajo.","Una ventaja es que hay cines.","Una ventaja es que hay mucho trabajo.","Una ventaja es que hay museos.","Una ventaja es el autobús.","Una ventaja son los museos.","Una ventaja son los cines.","Una ventaja es el metro"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-la-ventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “estar en contra” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"estar en contra","options":["to be against","to agree","to argue","to be right"]},"answer":"to be against","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-estar-en-contra"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Estoy en contra ___ plan.","translation":"I’m against the plan.","options":["del","de el","al","en"]},"answer":"del","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Estar en contra is followed by de, and de + el always contracts to del, just as a + el becomes al.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-estar-en-contra"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Mi hermano prefiere el campo; yo, en ___, prefiero la ciudad.","translation":"My brother prefers the countryside; I, on the other hand, prefer the city.","options":["cambio","contra","lado","casa"]},"answer":"cambio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"En cambio contrasts two people or things: mi hermano… yo, en cambio… En contra means against, and lado only works in por un lado / por otro lado.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-en-cambio"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":4,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"No quiero discutir contigo.","options":["No quiero discutir contigo.","No quiero discutir con ella.","No puedo discutir contigo.","No quiero hablar contigo."]},"answer":"No quiero discutir contigo.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-discutir"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":5,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"estar en contra","right":"to be against"},{"left":"en cambio","right":"whereas, by contrast"},{"left":"discutir","right":"to argue, to discuss"},{"left":"convencer","right":"to convince"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-estar-en-contra","es-en-cambio","es-discutir","es-convencer"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-debate","setting":"In a Spanish class in Monterrey, the teacher and three students debate working from home.","speakers":[{"name":"Profesora","voice":"a"},{"name":"Valeria","voice":"b"},{"name":"Andrés","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Profesora","text":"Hoy vamos a discutir un tema: trabajar desde casa. ¿Quién quiere opinar primero?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Yo. Por un lado, trabajar desde casa tiene muchas ventajas: no tienes que tomar el autobús y es más barato."},{"speaker":"Andrés","text":"Tienes razón, pero por otro lado, te sientes muy solo. Yo estoy en contra de trabajar siempre desde casa."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Para mí, la desventaja más grande es que casi no hablas con tu equipo."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"En cambio, en casa tengo más tiempo para mi familia y para hacer ejercicio."},{"speaker":"Profesora","text":"Muy bien. Andrés, ¿Valeria te convenció?"},{"speaker":"Andrés","text":"Un poco. Creo que lo mejor es trabajar dos días en casa y tres en la oficina."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"¡Estoy de acuerdo! Es la mejor solución."}]},"question":"What is Andrés’s position on working from home?","options":["He is against working from home all the time","He wants to work from home every day","He doesn’t have an opinion","He prefers to work on Sundays"]},"answer":"He is against working from home all the time","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Andrés says “por otro lado, te sientes muy solo. Yo estoy en contra de trabajar siempre desde casa”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-debate","setting":"In a Spanish class in Monterrey, the teacher and three students debate working from home.","speakers":[{"name":"Profesora","voice":"a"},{"name":"Valeria","voice":"b"},{"name":"Andrés","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Profesora","text":"Hoy vamos a discutir un tema: trabajar desde casa. ¿Quién quiere opinar primero?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Yo. Por un lado, trabajar desde casa tiene muchas ventajas: no tienes que tomar el autobús y es más barato."},{"speaker":"Andrés","text":"Tienes razón, pero por otro lado, te sientes muy solo. Yo estoy en contra de trabajar siempre desde casa."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Para mí, la desventaja más grande es que casi no hablas con tu equipo."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"En cambio, en casa tengo más tiempo para mi familia y para hacer ejercicio."},{"speaker":"Profesora","text":"Muy bien. Andrés, ¿Valeria te convenció?"},{"speaker":"Andrés","text":"Un poco. Creo que lo mejor es trabajar dos días en casa y tres en la oficina."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"¡Estoy de acuerdo! Es la mejor solución."}]},"question":"According to Paula, what is the biggest disadvantage?","options":["You hardly talk to your team","You spend more money","You have to take the bus","You have less time for your family"]},"answer":"You hardly talk to your team","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula says “la desventaja más grande es que casi no hablas con tu equipo”: casi no means hardly.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Put the words in order","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Mis","padres","están","en","contra","del","viaje"],"translation":"My parents are against the trip."},"answer":"Mis padres están en contra del viaje.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["es-estar-en-contra"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"My sister, on the other hand, prefers the city."},"answer":"Mi hermana, en cambio, prefiere la ciudad.","accepted_answers":["Mi hermana en cambio prefiere la ciudad.","En cambio, mi hermana prefiere la ciudad.","En cambio mi hermana prefiere la ciudad.","Mi hermana, por otro lado, prefiere la ciudad."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-en-cambio"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l02-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l02","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Estás en contra de trabajar los sábados?","translation":"Say that you are against it (use «estoy en contra»)."},"answer":"Sí, estoy en contra.","accepted_answers":["Estoy en contra.","Sí, estoy en contra de trabajar los sábados.","Sí, estoy en contra de eso.","Sí, estoy totalmente en contra.","Sí, estoy en contra"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-estar-en-contra"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev1","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “la desventaja” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"la desventaja","options":["disadvantage","if I had","respect","if it were, if I were"]},"answer":"disadvantage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-la-desventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev1","position":2,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"la ventaja","right":"advantage"},{"left":"estar en contra","right":"to be against"},{"left":"convencer","right":"to convince"},{"left":"en cambio","right":"however, on the other hand"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-la-ventaja","es-estar-en-contra","es-convencer","es-en-cambio"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev1","position":3,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"estar en contra","options":["estar en contra","la ventaja","por un lado","discutir"]},"answer":"estar en contra","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-estar-en-contra"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev1","position":4,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"however, on the other hand"},"answer":"en cambio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-en-cambio"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev1","position":5,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Write the whole word","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"c_n_e_c_r","hint":"to convince"},"answer":"convencer","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["es-convencer"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev1","position":6,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Estás en contra de trabajar los sábados?","translation":"Say that you are against it (use «estoy en contra»)."},"answer":"Sí, estoy en contra.","accepted_answers":["Estoy en contra.","Sí, estoy en contra de trabajar los sábados.","Sí, estoy en contra de eso.","Sí, estoy totalmente en contra.","Sí, estoy en contra"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-estar-en-contra"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev1","position":7,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “la ventaja” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"la ventaja","options":["advantage","friendship","to argue, to discuss","to convince"]},"answer":"advantage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_se