rs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"si tuviera","right":"if I had"},{"left":"si pudiera","right":"if I could"},{"left":"si fuera","right":"if it were, if I were"},{"left":"haría","right":"I would do"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-si-tuviera","es-si-pudiera","es-si-fuera","es-haria"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l03-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Si ___ tiempo, iría al gimnasio.","translation":"If I had time, I would go to the gym.","options":["tuviera","tengo","tendría","tuve"]},"answer":"tuviera","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"An unreal condition takes the imperfect subjunctive after si: si tuviera. The conditional (tendría) never goes after si, and si tengo is a real condition (si tengo tiempo, voy).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-si-tuviera","es-iria"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l03-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Si ___ cerca del mar, iría a la playa todos los días.","translation":"If I lived near the sea, I would go to the beach every day.","options":["viviera","vivo","viviría","vivía"]},"answer":"viviera","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Viviera follows the same pattern as tuviera: vivieron → viviera. After si, use it, not the conditional viviría (which goes in the other half) or the imperfect vivía.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-iria","es-si-tuviera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l03-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l03","position":4,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Si fuera más barato, iría.","options":["Si fuera más barato, iría.","Si fuera más caro, iría.","Si es más barato, voy.","Si fuera más barato, no iría."]},"answer":"Si fuera más barato, iría.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-si-fuera","es-iria"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l03-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l03","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"¿Qué ___ si tuvieras un mes de vacaciones?","translation":"What would you do if you had a month of vacation?","options":["harías","haces","hiciste","haría"]},"answer":"harías","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"For tú, the conditional adds -s: harías (you would do). Haría is the yo or él / ella form. Notice that tuviera also takes -s for tú: si tuvieras.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-haria","es-si-tuviera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l03-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-premio","setting":"Three friends in Puebla imagine what they would do with a lot of money.","speakers":[{"name":"Diego","voice":"a"},{"name":"Sofía","voice":"b"},{"name":"Nico","voice":"a"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Diego","text":"Oye, Sofía, si tuvieras mucho dinero, ¿qué harías?"},{"speaker":"Sofía","text":"Si tuviera mucho dinero, iría a Italia con toda mi familia."},{"speaker":"Diego","text":"¿Y tu trabajo? ¿Lo dejarías?"},{"speaker":"Sofía","text":"No, me gusta mucho. Pero si pudiera, trabajaría menos horas."},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Yo viviría en el campo, cerca del mar, en una casa grande."},{"speaker":"Diego","text":"Yo no haría nada. ¡Dormiría todo el día!"},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Si yo fuera tú, iría a Italia con Sofía. ¡Es un plan mucho mejor!"}]},"question":"What would Sofía do if she had a lot of money?","options":["Travel to Italy with her whole family","Buy a house in the countryside","Quit her job","Sleep all day"]},"answer":"Travel to Italy with her whole family","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Sofía says “Si tuviera mucho dinero, iría a Italia con toda mi familia”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l03-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-premio","setting":"Three friends in Puebla imagine what they would do with a lot of money.","speakers":[{"name":"Diego","voice":"a"},{"name":"Sofía","voice":"b"},{"name":"Nico","voice":"a"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Diego","text":"Oye, Sofía, si tuvieras mucho dinero, ¿qué harías?"},{"speaker":"Sofía","text":"Si tuviera mucho dinero, iría a Italia con toda mi familia."},{"speaker":"Diego","text":"¿Y tu trabajo? ¿Lo dejarías?"},{"speaker":"Sofía","text":"No, me gusta mucho. Pero si pudiera, trabajaría menos horas."},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Yo viviría en el campo, cerca del mar, en una casa grande."},{"speaker":"Diego","text":"Yo no haría nada. ¡Dormiría todo el día!"},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Si yo fuera tú, iría a Italia con Sofía. ¡Es un plan mucho mejor!"}]},"question":"What would Sofía change about her job?","options":["She would work fewer hours","She would quit it","She would work from home","She would ask for more money"]},"answer":"She would work fewer hours","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"She doesn’t want to quit (“No, me gusta mucho”), but says “si pudiera, trabajaría menos horas”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l03-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Put the words in order","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Iría","contigo","si","tuviera","tiempo"],"translation":"I would go with you if I had time."},"an