sentence":"Si ___ tiempo, iría al gimnasio.","translation":"If I had time, I would go to the gym.","options":["tuviera","tengo","tendría","tuve"]},"answer":"tuviera","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"An unreal condition takes the imperfect subjunctive after si: si tuviera. The conditional (tendría) never goes after si, and si tengo is a real condition (si tengo tiempo, voy).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-si-tuviera","es-iria"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev2-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev2","position":4,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"respect"},"answer":"el respeto","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-el-respeto"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev2-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev2","position":5,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “confiar” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"confiar","options":["to trust","on the other hand","to argue, to discuss","respect"]},"answer":"to trust","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-confiar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev2-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev2","position":6,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Write the whole word","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"l_ a_i_t_d","hint":"friendship"},"answer":"la amistad","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["es-la-amistad"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev2-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev2","position":7,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “si fuera” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"si fuera","options":["if it were, if I were","friendship","on the other hand","if I could"]},"answer":"if it were, if I were","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-si-fuera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev2-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev2","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Puedo confiar en ti?","translation":"Say yes, they can trust you (use «puedes confiar en mí»)."},"answer":"Sí, puedes confiar en mí.","accepted_answers":["Puedes confiar en mí.","Claro, puedes confiar en mí.","Sí, claro, puedes confiar en mí.","Claro que sí, puedes confiar en mí.","Sí, puedes confiar en mí","Sí, podés confiar en mí."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-confiar"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev2-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev2","position":9,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Puedes ___ en mí.","translation":"You can trust me.","options":["confiar","confío","convencer"]},"answer":"confiar","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"After puedes, use the infinitive: puedes confiar. Confiar goes with en (confiar en alguien); convencer takes a, not en (convencer a alguien).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-confiar","es-convencer"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-rev2-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-rev2","position":10,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Match each word with its meaning","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"si fuera","right":"if it were, if I were"},{"left":"si pudiera","right":"if I could"},{"left":"la amistad","right":"friendship"},{"left":"el respeto","right":"respect"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-si-fuera","es-si-pudiera","es-la-amistad","es-el-respeto"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":1,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-foro","document":"post","setting":"Three people answer a question in an online forum.","title":"¿Vivir en la ciudad o en el campo?","lines":["Valeria, de Ciudad de México: Para mí, la ciudad tiene más ventajas: hay trabajo, cines y museos.","En cambio, en el campo casi no hay nada que hacer.","Andrés, de Oaxaca: No estoy de acuerdo. Yo vivo en un pueblo y estoy en contra de la vida en la ciudad: hay mucho ruido y mucho estrés.","En mi pueblo, puedes confiar en tus vecinos.","Paula, de Lima: Por un lado, me encanta la ciudad; por otro lado, si pudiera, viviría en el campo con mis perros.","Si tuviera un trabajo desde casa, me iría mañana."]},"question":"Why does Valeria prefer the city?","options":["There is work, there are cinemas and museums","It is quiet","People trust their neighbors","It is cheaper"]},"answer":"There is work, there are cinemas and museums","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Valeria writes “la ciudad tiene más ventajas: hay trabajo, cines y museos”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":2,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-foro","document":"post","setting":"Three people answer a question in an online forum.","title":"¿Vivir en la ciudad o en el campo?","lines":["Valeria, de Ciudad de México: Para mí, la ciudad tiene más ventajas: hay trabajo, cines y museos.","En cambio, en el campo casi no hay nada que hacer.","Andrés, de Oaxaca: No estoy de acuerdo. Yo vivo en un pueblo y estoy en contra de la vida en la ciudad: hay mucho ruido y mucho estrés.","En mi pueblo, puedes confiar en tus vecinos.","Paula, de Lima: Por un lado, me encanta la ciudad; por otro lado, si pudiera, viviría en el campo con mis perros.","Si tuviera un trabajo desde casa, me iría mañana."]},"question":"What does Andrés like about his town?","options":["You can trust your neighbors","There is a lot of work","There are many cinemas","It is near the sea"]},"answer":"You can trust your neighbors","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Andrés is against city life because of the noise and stress, and writes “En mi pueblo, puedes confiar en tus vecinos”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":3,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-foro","document":"post","setting":"Three people answer a question in an online forum.","title":"¿Vivir en la ciudad o en el campo?","lines":["Valeria, de Ciudad de México: Para mí, la ciudad tiene más ventajas: hay trabajo, cines y museos.","En cambio, en el campo casi no hay nada que hacer.","Andrés, de Oaxaca: No estoy de acuerdo. Yo vivo en un pueblo y estoy en contra de la vida en la ciudad: hay mucho ruido y mucho estrés.","En mi pueblo, puedes confiar en tus vecinos.","Paula, de Lima: Por un lado, me encanta la ciudad; por otro lado, si pudiera, viviría en el campo con mis perros.","Si tuviera un trabajo desde casa, me iría mañana."]},"question":"What would Paula need to move to the countryside?","options":["A job she could do from home","More dogs","A bigger house in the city","Her family’s permission"]},"answer":"A job she could do from home","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula writes “Si tuviera un trabajo desde casa, me iría mañana”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-respuesta","document":"email","setting":"Carmen answers Mateo’s letter in her advice column.","from":"Carmen","to":"Mateo","lines":["Querido Mateo:","Gracias por confiar en mí.","Para mí, una amistad sin respeto no es una amistad.","Si yo fuera tú, hablaría con Rodrigo y le diría cómo te sientes.","Por un lado, él tiene mucho trabajo; por otro lado, tu tiempo también es importante.","Si es un buen amigo, no va a cancelar más planes.","Mucha suerte."]},"question":"According to Carmen, what is a friendship without respect?","options":["It isn’t really a friendship","The best kind of friendship","A normal friendship","A problem that is easy to fix"]},"answer":"It isn’t really a friendship","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Carmen writes “una amistad sin respeto no es una amistad”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":50,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e05","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-premio","setting":"Three friends in Puebla imagine what they would do with a lot of money.","speakers":[{"name":"Diego","voice":"a"},{"name":"Sofía","voice":"b"},{"name":"Nico","voice":"a"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Diego","text":"Oye, Sofía, si tuvieras mucho dinero, ¿qué harías?"},{"speaker":"Sofía","text":"Si tuviera mucho dinero, iría a Italia con toda mi familia."},{"speaker":"Diego","text":"¿Y tu trabajo? ¿Lo dejarías?"},{"speaker":"Sofía","text":"No, me gusta mucho. Pero si pudiera, trabajaría menos horas."},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Yo viviría en el campo, cerca del mar, en una casa grande."},{"speaker":"Diego","text":"Yo no haría nada. ¡Dormiría todo el día!"},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Si yo fuera tú, iría a Italia con Sofía. ¡Es un plan mucho mejor!"}]},"question":"What would Diego do with a lot of money?","options":["Nothing: he would sleep all day","Travel to Italy","Live in the countryside","Work fewer hours"]},"answer":"Nothing: he would sleep all day","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Diego says “Yo no haría nada. ¡Dormiría todo el día!”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e06","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.b1-u11-debate","setting":"In a Spanish class in Monterrey, the teacher and three students debate working from home.","speakers":[{"name":"Profesora","voice":"a"},{"name":"Valeria","voice":"b"},{"name":"Andrés","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.95,"lines":[{"speaker":"Profesora","text":"Hoy vamos a discutir un tema: trabajar desde casa. ¿Quién quiere opinar primero?"},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"Yo. Por un lado, trabajar desde casa tiene muchas ventajas: no tienes que tomar el autobús y es más barato."},{"speaker":"Andrés","text":"Tienes razón, pero por otro lado, te sientes muy solo. Yo estoy en contra de trabajar siempre desde casa."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Para mí, la desventaja más grande es que casi no hablas con tu equipo."},{"speaker":"Valeria","text":"En cambio, en casa tengo más tiempo para mi familia y para hacer ejercicio."},{"speaker":"Profesora","text":"Muy bien. Andrés, ¿Valeria te convenció?"},{"speaker":"Andrés","text":"Un poco. Creo que lo mejor es trabajar dos días en casa y tres en la oficina."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"¡Estoy de acuerdo! Es la mejor solución."}]},"question":"What does Andrés propose at the end of the debate?","options":["Working two days at home and three at the office","Working from home every day","Working only at the office","Working on Saturdays"]},"answer":"Working two days at home and three at the office","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"When the teacher asks “¿Valeria te convenció?”, Andrés says “Un poco. Creo que lo mejor es trabajar dos días en casa y tres en la oficina”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e07","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":7,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Me ___: ahora estoy de acuerdo contigo.","translation":"You’ve convinced me: now I agree with you.","options":["convenciste","convencer","confiar"]},"answer":"convenciste","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Convenciste is the tú form of the preterite of convencer: me convenciste (you convinced me). After me you need a conjugated verb, not an infinitive.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-convencer"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e08","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Tienes razón, pero estoy en contra.","options":["Tienes razón, pero estoy en contra.","No tienes razón, estoy en contra.","Tienes razón, pero estoy de acuerdo.","Tienes razón, estoy en contra."]},"answer":"Tienes razón, pero estoy en contra.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-estar-en-contra"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e09","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"If I could, I would live in the countryside."},"answer":"Si pudiera, viviría en el campo.","accepted_answers":["Si pudiera viviría en el campo.","Viviría en el campo si pudiera.","Si yo pudiera, viviría en el campo.","Si pudiese, viviría en el campo."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-si-pudiera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-l05-e10","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-l05","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Qué harías si tuvieras un mes libre?","translation":"Say what you would do, for example go to Oaxaca (use «iría» or «haría»)."},"answer":"Iría a Oaxaca.","accepted_answers":["Si tuviera un mes libre, iría a Oaxaca.","Yo iría a Oaxaca.","Iría a la playa.","Iría a Italia.","Iría a México.","Haría un viaje.","Haría un viaje a Oaxaca.","Si tuviera un mes libre, haría un viaje.","Iría a la playa con mi familia.","Iría a Oaxaca"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-iria","es-haria","es-si-tuviera"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-listen-e01","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-listen","position":1,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Una ventaja es el precio.","options":["Una ventaja es el precio.","Una desventaja es el precio.","Una ventaja es el clima.","La ventaja es el precio."]},"answer":"Una ventaja es el precio.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-la-ventaja","es-la-desventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-listen-e02","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-listen","position":2,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"la ventaja","options":["la ventaja","haría","la desventaja","iría"]},"answer":"la ventaja","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-la-ventaja"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-listen-e03","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-listen","position":3,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"por un lado","options":["por un lado","opinar","la desventaja","si fuera"]},"answer":"por un lado","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-por-un-lado"]},{"id":"es-b1-u11-listen-e04","lesson_id":"es-b1-u11-listen","position":4,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"si fuera","options":["si fuera","el respeto","por un lado","discutir"]},"answer":"si fuera","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"d