llovía","llueve","llover"]},"answer":"llovía","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The weather and the time are the scene of the story, so they go in the imperfect: era de noche, llovía. What happens next goes in the preterite: llegué.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"es.ex.w0ngysi805bc27","content_hash":"v1:4a2bdfed16154168b05a6f659c0a03b53d13f2e64b137cbf3b4c68c92c7afddb","prompt_es":"Put the words in order","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Mi","abuelo","siempre","cuenta","historias","divertidas"],"translation":"My grandfather always tells funny stories."},"answer":"Mi abuelo siempre cuenta historias divertidas.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"grading_spec":{"mode":"normalized_text","mode_version":1,"normalizer":"polygo.answers.v1","typo_tolerance":false},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"es.ex.0n7beabrsdxyf4","content_hash":"v1:e5211a789761cbf0b4b93bdbdc0a143856830de8ae584e2cecd58e884e2b9d52","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"It was a very funny story."},"answer":"Fue una historia muy divertida.","accepted_answers":["Era una historia muy divertida.","Fue una anécdota muy divertida.","Era una anécdota muy divertida."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"grading_spec":{"mode":"normalized_text","mode_version":1,"normalizer":"polygo.answers.v1","typo_tolerance":true},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"es.ex.5fkx2yejp1h7o7","content_hash":"v1:14bbebbe85485713ba8ffa2c66ea4e12d76fc6d4af14a93c85b2bff37d124fb1","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Qué te pasó? Estás muy contento.","translation":"Say that something very funny happened to you (use «me pasó»)."},"answer":"Me pasó algo muy divertido.","accepted_answers":["Me pasó algo dive